  "body": "Was stacked on #1123 (on #560, #551); all three have merged to main, and this PR now targets main with only its own files (`git diff upstream/main --stat`: 20 files). The codes live on `Machine.edm_codes`; main's `edm.rs` changes by one line only (`codes` joins `COMMON_KEYS`, so main's key law admits `edm.codes`).\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`assets/posts/wire-iso.cps`** (\"Generic ISO Wire EDM\", #290 D5). It posts the 2-axis Wire Contour in RS-274 / ISO 6983 words: `%`, G21/G20, G90, G17, the work offset, G0/G1/G2/G3 (incremental I J), M00/M01, M30. Every EDM-specific code comes from the machine's `.mch` `edm.codes`: `condition` (a template holding `{id}`), `comp_off`, and, when `edm.awt: true`, `thread`, `cut` and `tip_disposal`. Each missing code refuses the post as \"machine <m> states no edm.codes.<x>\". Without AWT the post writes M00 so the operator can thread the wire at the start and cut it at the end.\n- **Kerf vs pre-offset path (#532's decision):** the op's moves are already the wire-centre path. The post therefore cancels compensation before every cut and never engages it, so the kerf is applied only once. The post writes no F word, because the condition sets the cutting rate.\n- **Refusals by name:** a machine that is not `kind: wire_edm`, a rapid while the wire is threaded, a Z change, a posed move, an arc off the XY plane, a cycle, a tool change, a spindle speed, and a section that is not wire work.\n- **post crate:**\n  - `machine/edm_codes.rs` parses `edm.codes`; a garbled entry refuses the file by name.\n  - The mirror and `script_props` expose `machine.kind` and `machine.edm = {codes, awt}` for EDM kinds.\n  - New engine door: `PARAM EdmCondition` through a script without the `wireEdm = true` manifest flag is refused by name, so no cutting post can post a wire path.\n- **app:**\n  - `posting_wire.rs` streams the op's section (`EdmCondition`, `WireSide`, no TOOL or spindle).\n  - The post is in `BUILTINS`, and `WIRE_POSTS` serves `wire_edm` only. It is the default post for a wire EDM, and no cutting post serves a wire EDM.\n  - `op_streams` no longer refuses the Wire Contour. Any other tool-less kind is still refused.\n- Docs: `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`, `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` (the PARAMs). The decision record is `docs/decisions/533-wire-iso-post.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `wire_post.rs` (new):\n  - `the_punch_contour_posts_its_golden_through_the_gate`: the full `posting::post_script` gate, verification included, matches the golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/wire-iso/wire_slug_punch.nc` (renamed from `wire_contour_punch.nc` in the refresh: it is posted from this suite's own slug document, not from the `wire_contour_punch.cl` golden, and main's posted-golden guard (#1093) reads a shared stem as that `.cl`'s posting). It also checks the order G0 -> thread -> condition -> comp off -> cut -> wire cut -> tip disposal, and that there is no Z, F, G41/G42 or spindle word.\n  - `each_required_code_removed_refuses_the_post_by_name`: removing each of the 5 codes refuses by name. A machine without AWT posts with two M00 stops and needs no AWT codes. A condition template without `{id}` is refused.\n  - `a_mill_machine_and_a_cutting_post_are_refused_by_name`: the VMC machine is refused, every other built-in post is refused the wire section (`wireEdm`), and a mill golden through the wire post is refused.\n  - `the_registry_offers_the_wire_post_for_wire_edms_only`\n- Synthetic fixture `crates/app/tests/edm/wire-iso-fixture.mch`: the codes are clearly fictional (`FX-THREAD`, `FX-COND {id}` ...) and the condition is invented.\n- Updated: `wire_contour.rs` (the op now streams with its condition, where it used to be refused), `conformance.rs` (the registry, extension tables).\n- Unit test in `edm_codes.rs`.\n- Refresh gate on 31ac7556 (merge of main 9f8defc1): `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green - post suites (24 binaries, 33 s) and every app suite (782 s; the renamed golden is shared test input), 0 failed, including `solid_law_goldens::every_posted_golden_is_a_program_the_gate_passes`, `wire_post`, `wire_contour`, `conformance`; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. The wire golden's bytes are unchanged (pure rename).\n- Earlier gate on b9ddec58: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/issue/532-wire-contour` green - post suites (lib, axis_direction_cli, comp, comp_plane, mch_head_search, post_engine) and every app suite (the new golden is shared test input, so quick ran the whole app set), 0 failed; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n### Review fix @ 58b40b53 (main e74bca1f merged)\n- `posting_family::edm_at_post` (#1131): `Kind::WireEdm` now passes the door (`continue`); `Kind::SinkerEdm` is still refused by name (#542). Doc comments at the door, its three callers and `posting_serves` updated.\n- New pins in `wire_post.rs`: `a_wire_setup_missing_a_code_is_refused_by_name_through_post_script` (each `edm.codes.<x>` refused through `post_script`, no file written) and `a_sinker_setup_is_still_refused_at_post_by_name` (#542 text from every registry post, no file written).\n- Main's per-script-suite law: `crates/post/tests/script_wire_iso.rs` plus 11 recorded goldens under `recorded/golden/wire-iso/`. All 11 are named refusals, since none of the recorded streams is wire work.\n- Gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` shows post suites ok and app suites ok, with one exception: `stepped_stock_rapid::a_coarse_stock_whose_source_is_gone_is_never_acquitted`. That test fails the same way on plain upstream/main e74bca1f, outside this diff, and is filed as #1336. `every_posted_golden_is_a_program_the_gate_passes`, `wire_post`, `sinker_burn_held` and `recorded_streams` are green. Clippy `-D warnings` (post, app, all targets) is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **Not exercised on a real EDM control (#290 D10).** The golden is posted against the synthetic fixture dialect. A user with a real machine fills `edm.codes` from its manual and dry-runs before any cut.\n- No wire verification yet (#534). No taper, 4-axis or skims. No UI for editing `edm.codes` (they are hand-stated in the `.mch` for now). The CLI raw-machine door passes `edm` through unvalidated, and the script validates each code it reads.\n\nChangelog: Wire EDM: a generic ISO wire post (\"Generic ISO Wire EDM\") posts the 2-axis Wire Contour, with every EDM code (condition, compensation cancel, AWT thread/cut, wire-tip disposal) taken from the machine's `edm.codes` and refused by name when missing (#533)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #533\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
